# Security & Secrets

## Never commit secrets
- Do not commit API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, OAuth client secrets, or connection strings.
- Do not paste real secrets into code, tests, screenshots, commits, or chat logs.
- Prefer environment variables, CI/CD secret stores, or platform-specific secure storage for runtime secrets.

## Files and paths
- Treat `.env`, `.env.*`, `*.pem`, `*service-account*.json`, and similar as sensitive; never add real values to the repo.
- If an example config is needed, commit `.env.example` with placeholder names only.

## Flutter / mobile
- Use `flutter_secure_storage` or platform keychains for tokens on device when applicable; avoid `SharedPreferences` for secrets.

## Dependencies and supply chain
- Prefer well-maintained packages; review changelog and trust before adding new dependencies.
- After adding or upgrading packages, run analyzer/tests; report known CVEs if upgrading cannot wait.

## Future APIs
- Validate and sanitize all external input (HTTP bodies, query params, file uploads).
- Use HTTPS in production; pin or verify certificates if the app implements custom networking.
